# OKX / 欧意 Surge 完整稳定规则集
# Version: 2026-10-06 R2
# Source:
#   1) Surge Archive actual traffic: 2026-10-06 12:56
#   2) Surge Archive actual traffic: 2026-10-06 13:12
#   3) Compatibility domains from current/public OKX rule references
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - This is a RULE-SET file. Do NOT append a policy name to lines below.
# - In [Rule], place this RULE-SET ABOVE generic proxy sets such as Proxy_All_No_Resolve.list.
# - macOS process rules provide the final safety net for OKX dynamic/raw-IP connections.
# - iOS ignores PROCESS-NAME, so domain coverage below is intentionally broader than R1.

# ============================================================
# 0. macOS catch-all
# ============================================================
# App-bundle mode (Surge Mac 6+): catches all executables inside OKX.app.
PROCESS-NAME,/Applications/OKX.app/
# Filename fallback: catches OKX and OKX Helper style process names.
PROCESS-NAME,OKX*

# ============================================================
# 1. OKX first-party / primary infrastructure
# ============================================================
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okx.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okx.cab
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okx.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okex.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okex.me
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okmac.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okcoin.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,coinall.ltd
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,oklink.com

# OKX DNS / bootstrap domains
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okx-dns.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okx-dns1.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,okx-dns2.com

# Future/variant safety net for hostnames containing OKX/OKEX.
DOMAIN-KEYWORD,okx
DOMAIN-KEYWORD,okex

# ============================================================
# 2. OKX alternate / failover domains observed in real traffic
# ============================================================
# API / web gateway
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,qqhrss.com

# WebSocket primary / derivatives failover groups
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,gihiji.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,yiym1eo.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,ouyich.biz
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,ouyich.show

# Static / bootstrap mirrors
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,jingyunyilian.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,yqtjc.cn

# ============================================================
# 3. OKX direct distribution endpoint observed in real traffic
# ============================================================
DOMAIN,okg-pub-hk.oss-cn-hongkong.aliyuncs.com

# ============================================================
# 4. Functional shared dependencies observed from OKX
#    Exact-host rules are used to reduce cross-app overmatching.
# ============================================================
# CAPTCHA / verification
DOMAIN,dkapi-ga.geetest.com
DOMAIN,www.recaptcha.net

# Risk / device verification
DOMAIN,aa.online-metrix.net

# Embedded market/chart component
DOMAIN,www.tradingview-widget.com

# ============================================================
# 5. Legacy OKX wallet compatibility
# ============================================================
DOMAIN,wallet.okex.org

# ============================================================
# Intentionally excluded from dedicated OKX routing
# ============================================================
# The following appeared in OKX traffic but are shared analytics,
# advertising or generic Google/TikTok/Yandex infrastructure.
# They should stay under your normal global proxy rules instead of
# being forced into the OKX policy:
#
# mc.yandex.ru
# analytics.tiktok.com
# analytics-ipv6.tiktokw.us
# www.googletagmanager.com
# www.google-analytics.com
# analytics.google.com
# ad.doubleclick.net
# googleads.g.doubleclick.net
# stats.g.doubleclick.net
# www.googleadservices.com
# www.google.com
# www.google.co.jp
# www.gstatic.com
#
# Also intentionally NOT added:
# - raw OKX destination IPs seen without SNI
# - CloudFront/AliCDN/CNAME parent networks
# Those addresses are dynamic/shared. On macOS PROCESS-NAME catches them;
# hard-coding shared IP ranges would make the rule set less stable, not more.
